    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "After a medical entrance exam was held on May 3, a whistleblower in Sikar sent an email to India's National Testing Agency with proof of a leak matching the exam paper. This tip-off exposed a completely compromised exam system, leading to the cancellation of NEET-UG 2026 and the referral of twenty-six to twenty-seven paper setters and translators to the CBI for investigation.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Outlaw",
        "fragments": [
          "how-0",
          "how-1",
          "why-0",
          "result-0",
          "how-2"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.85
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "The state's investigative arm moved to restore order, rounding up suspects and arresting thirteen individuals. Among them was a former champion for student justice, now implicated in the scandal. The system, facing a major outcome, scheduled a forced do-over: a re-examination to be held on June 21 in a desperate bid to regain legitimacy.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Outlaw",
        "fragments": [
          "how-3",
          "result-1",
          "how-4",
          "result-2"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.78
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "The downfall of the entire corrupt exam began with evidence from a single informant, a truth-teller against the corrupt exam system. His disclosure forced the gatekeeper of the compromised testing system to point the finger at its own personnel. While multiple individuals were taken into custody, the true victory was exposing the rotten machinery, not the arrests themselves.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Outlaw",
